---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import Container from '../components/ui/Container.astro';
import Heading from '../components/ui/Heading.astro';
---

<Layout title='About Me | Rokas'>
  <main id='main' class='w-full pb-24 pt-36 sm:pt-44'>
    <Container size='narrow'>
      <a
        href='/#about'
        class='text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-muted transition duration-200 hover:text-primary'
        >← Back home</a
      >
      <Heading as='h1' size='display' class='mt-5'>More about me</Heading>
      <div class='mt-6 h-px w-16 bg-accent/60'></div>
      <div class='mt-10 space-y-6 text-base leading-7 text-secondary'>
        <p>
          Hi, my name is Rokas. I'm a front-end engineer with nearly 4 years of hands-on experience
          building modern, high-performance web applications. I'm self-taught. I've been programming
          since high school, spent two years at "Jaunųjų informatikų akademija", and turned that
          curiosity into a career of shipping production software. That background shaped how I work:
          I learn fast, take ownership, and don't wait for someone to hand me a spec.
        </p>
        <p>
          At my current role I'm regularly <b class='font-medium text-primary'>trusted to lead our largest
          initiatives</b> as the go-to engineer for architectural decisions, technical planning, and
          implementation strategy on complex features. I led the <b class='font-medium text-primary'>end-to-end redesign</b>
          of a major gaming-industry website, building a scalable, theme-driven design system along the
          way. As the sole front-end engineer on an R&D initiative, I independently
          delivered a complete prototype of a <b class='font-medium text-primary'>real-time component
          library</b> with WebSocket integration and an embeddable script. In between, I refactor legacy
          code toward modern <b class='font-medium text-primary'>React</b> patterns, improving
          performance, SEO, and long-term maintainability.
        </p>
        <p>
          Outside of work I keep building. Right now I'm working on
          <b class='font-medium text-primary'>Sinwy</b>, a SaaS platform where businesses build their
          public pages with a CMS page builder and customers discover and browse them. It's a full
          stack <b class='font-medium text-primary'>TypeScript</b> app: a backend server that handles
          the business logic (organizations, users, payments and subscriptions, calendars and
          bookings, the CMS), and a React frontend built with
          <b class='font-medium text-primary'>module federation</b>, split into a business owner
          dashboard with the page builder and a customer-facing platform for finding services. Once
          the core platform ships, the next step on my roadmap is a custom AI agent inside the app
          to help owners build their pages and make sense of their bookings, revenue, and analytics.
          I gravitate toward the <b class='font-medium text-primary'>React and TypeScript</b>
          ecosystem, but I treat languages and frameworks as tools. What I care about is engineering:
          understanding the problem, choosing the right approach, and shipping something that lasts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class='mt-12 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-6'>
        <Button href='/CV.pdf' download>Download CV ↓</Button>
        <Button href='/#contact' variant='ghost'>Get in touch →</Button>
      </div>
    </Container>
  </main>
</Layout>
